course: dictionary
lesson: 6123
title: A cloud of midges
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A midge is a tiny flying insect, so small that you might mistake it for a speck of dust. The clues are in the words around it. «On a summer evening over a pond you can watch bats swoop and twist after midges.» Midges fly near water, and bats hunt them, so they must be small flying insects.
explain: «A small bat can catch hundreds of midges in an hour.» Hundreds tells you there are huge numbers of them, and a bat can eat them. Always ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some midges bite. «Campers in Scotland use midge repellent» tells you that a midge can be a nuisance, so people need something to keep them away. Repellent is a clue too: a thing that repels pushes something away.
fact: A midge is a tiny flying insect, often seen in clouds near water.
fact: Some midges bite people, and the Highland midge is famous for biting on summer evenings in Scotland.
fact: «Midge bites» are the itchy marks left after a midge bites you.
fact: Midges are food for birds, bats and fish.
fact: A small bat can catch hundreds of midges in an hour, so bats help to control pests.
exercise: «A small bat can catch hundreds of midges in an hour.» What is a midge? | A large bird that lives near lakes | *A tiny flying insect | A small fish with fins | A type of bat that sleeps all day
exercise: Where do midges often gather? | On the tops of mountains | *In clouds near water | Under the sea | Inside houses at midnight
exercise: Some midges bite, so people use «midge repellent». What does repellent most likely mean? | A pond where midges live | *Something that keeps midges away | A sweet cake | A food that bats like to eat
test: «Campers in Scotland use midge spray and nets.» Why do campers use midge spray? | To attract midges | To feed the midges | *To keep midges away from their skin | To make a cake
test: Which of these animals eats midges? | A rock | A sofa | *A bat | A cow
exam: Read: «One pipistrelle can eat thousands of midges in a night.» What does this tell you about midges? | They never fly | *They are small and plentiful, a meal for bats | They live in deserts | They are very large
